<title>BELGIUM: W.Europe car registrations in February - table.</title>
<headline>W.Europe car registrations in February - table.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are provisional West European new car registrations and market share figures for February released by the European Automobile Manufacturers</p>
<p>Association (ACEA) on Thursday.</p>
<p>  Brand		    Feb 97   pct change  mkt share vs Feb 96</p>
<p>							   (pct)	 (pct)</p>
<p>All brands	   1,039,300   -1.3</p>
<p>Volkswagen	     183,500   +4.2	    17.7	 16.7</p>
<p>Fiat		     136,800   +4.3	    13.2	 12.5</p>
<p>GM			 125,469   -4.6	    12.1	 12.5</p>
<p>PSA			121,567   -9.6	    11.7	 12.8</p>
<p>Japanese		 118,079   +10.3	   11.4	 10.2</p>
<p>Ford		     106,340   -15.7	   10.2	 12.0</p>
<p>Renault		  103,639   -2.9	    10.0	 10.1</p>
<p>BMW			 59,583   +1.4	     5.7	  5.6</p>
<p>Mercedes		  33,500   -5.4	     3.2	  3.4</p>
<p>Korean		    20,260   +16.0	    1.9	  1.7</p>
<p>Volvo		     19,807   +29.8	    1.9	  1.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Volkswagen includes Audi, Seat, Skoda; GM includes Opel/Vauxhall, U.S. imports, Saab, IBC /ISUZU ; Ford includes U.S. imports, Jaguar; Fiat includes Lancia, Alfa Romeo, Innocenti, Ferrari, Maserati; PSA includes Peugeot, Citroen; Japanese includes Nissan, Toyota, Mazda, Honda, Mitsubishi, others; BMW includes Rover; ACEA provides no breakdown for the Korean figures.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6830, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
